152	/// A value that the scheduler returns to the guest when resuming.  This is weakly typed in that it
153	/// is only relevant to certain scheduler requests, and its meaning is dependent on what was
154	/// requested of the scheduler.
155	///
156	/// It can be used to have the scheduler EMULATE behaviors (syscalls) that would normally happen in
157	/// the guest. The first application for this is futexes.
158	pub enum SchedValue {
159	    /// The action timed out while waiting on the scheduler.
160	    TimeOut,
161	    // TODO(T137799529) make this more strongly typed, an enum for different scenarios:
